From 23546df26e813704f2c405b48c70866173d93f29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 4evy <git@evy.pink>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0300
Subject: git push: warn about immutable signing candidates

Evaluate the configured sign-on-push revset across every outgoing commit, then exclude immutable matches from rewriting and list them in a warning. This follows the same immutability boundary as other history-editing commands while making skipped signatures visible.

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index a78138b2ba2dccb8741be00f6a80e9d665c9efac..7f5a02a54e38002ae2dce30472d57dfabd9d36aa 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -135,6 +135,9 @@ None
   when the commit stack is taller than the terminal.
   [#9033](https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/issues/9033).
 
+* `jj git push` now warns when `git.sign-on-push` selects immutable commits
+  instead of silently leaving them unsigned.
+
 * The default pager flags now include `-K` (`--quit-on-intr`), so pressing
   Ctrl+C in `less` exits cleanly instead of leaving the terminal in a
   corrupted state (raw mode, visible escape sequences, broken input).
diff --git a/cli/src/commands/git/push.rs b/cli/src/commands/git/push.rs
index 208d3d11bfd6436a66eb5ae9dc913d01b4620424..e2b74e925a76c6e2f8aa3549b10431ca3348f889 100644
--- a/cli/src/commands/git/push.rs
+++ b/cli/src/commands/git/push.rs
@@ -905,7 +905,8 @@ fn ready_to_push_revset_expression(
 
 /// Signs commits before pushing.
 ///
-/// Warns about commits that need a signature but are immutable.
+/// Warns about selected commits that are immutable and therefore cannot be
+/// rewritten.
 ///
 /// Returns the updated list of bookmark names and corresponding
 /// [`BookmarkPushUpdate`]s.
